# 25. SECURITY NOTIFICATIONS

Administrators should receive email notifications for important security events.

At minimum:

```text
Successful login
Failed login
Password changed
Password reset
New administrator created
Administrator role changed
Administrator account disabled
```

---

# 26. ADMIN LOGIN EMAIL

Send an email after successful administrator login.

Example subject:

```text
New SMEvolve Admin Login
```

The email should contain:

```text
Administrator
Date & Time
IP Address
Approximate Location
Device
Browser
Operating System
Action
```

---

# 27. FAILED LOGIN EMAIL

For failed logins, send security notifications according to a reasonable threshold.

Do not send an email for every single failed attempt if doing so could create an email flood.

Recommended approach:

```text
Normal failed attempt
        ↓
Audit Log

Repeated/suspicious attempts
        ↓
Security Email
```

---

# 28. SUSPICIOUS LOGIN DETECTION

Where practical, identify potentially unusual login activity.

Examples:

```text
New device
Unusual location
Repeated failed attempts
Rapid login attempts
```

Do not automatically classify legitimate activity as malicious.

Label events as:

```text
Unusual activity
```

rather than making unsupported security claims.

